# ops/Dockerfile.web — the Caddy that holds the hostname, and the dist/ that
# passed the cross-engine gate.
#
# THIS IMAGE BUILDS NOTHING, AND THAT ABSENCE IS THE WHOLE POINT. `dist/` is
# downloaded from the artifact the CI `test` job uploaded, so what is published
# is BYTE FOR BYTE what cleared the determinism gate in Chromium, Firefox and
# WebKit (D2-05, preserved by D2-23). A multi-stage Dockerfile that ran
# `npm run build` here would be shorter to write and would annul phase 1
# entirely: the bytes a player downloads would be the output of a build nobody
# gated. The build context is the repository root, so the two COPY paths below
# read as they are written.
#
# WHY THERE IS NO `USER` HERE, AND IT IS A DECISION RATHER THAN AN OVERSIGHT.
# ops/Dockerfile.api drops to a non-root user because it opens a database on a
# persistent volume; neither half of that reasoning applies here. Caddy writes
# to its own data directory on boot, the alpine image ships no unprivileged
# user with that directory prepared, and this container publishes no port on the
# host, mounts no volume and opens no database. What `USER` buys in the api is
# containment of a process that touches durable state — there is no durable
# state on this side. Declared here so the next reader finds a reason instead of
# an omission.
#
# The tag is an EXACT PATCH VERSION and never `latest` (C-6, T-2-SC). The known
# improvement — pinning by digest — is registered in ops/README.md rather than
# discovered later: a patch tag is still a name the publisher can move, and the
# day that matters is the day it moves to something hostile.
FROM caddy:2.11.4-alpine

# The config path the image's own default CMD already reads, which is why this
# image overrides no command. ops/Caddyfile is the file plan 02-13 wrote: the
# global block, the four security headers the Traefik of Coolify does not send
# (DM-11), the three cache matchers, and the deliberate absence of try_files.
COPY ops/Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile

# The static root, and it has to agree with `root * /srv/www` in the Caddyfile.
# Disagree and the container serves an empty directory: every request a 404,
# with Caddy healthy and nothing in any log saying why. A test compares the two
# files for exactly that reason.
COPY dist/ /srv/www/
